From 57f9233c91b2006eb5ccf1f45987ccf247544397 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bmatusiak <bmatusiak@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:26:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] okcore: a second PIN added in config mode keeps the profile
 key readable

One profile key encrypts the slots and keys of both profiles. It is
stored wrapped under a hash of the nonce2 mask, the chip ID, a
Curve25519 shared secret and the nonce, and an unlock picks the shared
secret by the second-profile mode: STDPROFILE2 uses the primary PIN key
with the second PIN key, any other mode the primary PIN key with itself.

okcore_flashset_2ndpinhashpublic() re-wraps the profile key under the
two-PIN secret whenever a second PIN is set, but recorded STDPROFILE2
only while the key was being set up (!initcheck). On a key set up with
its primary PIN alone and given a second PIN later in config mode, the
mode stays as it was. The next unlock with the primary PIN still passes
(the PIN hash does not involve the profile key) and unwraps the profile
key with the one-profile secret, so every slot and key it protects -
the derivation keys included - is read as something else.

Record STDPROFILE2 whenever a second PIN is set on an encrypted second
profile. A first setup is unchanged; a non-encrypted second profile
(NONENCRYPTEDPROFILE) is untouched.
---
 onlykey/okcore.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/onlykey/okcore.cpp b/onlykey/okcore.cpp
index 0620dbc..44c08c1 100644
--- a/onlykey/okcore.cpp
+++ b/onlykey/okcore.cpp
@@ -3165,7 +3165,12 @@ void okcore_flashset_2ndpinhashpublic(uint8_t *ptr) {
     okeeprom_eeget_2ndprofilemode(&p2mode);
     if (p2mode != NONENCRYPTEDPROFILE) { //profile key not used for plausible deniability mode or international fw
 #ifdef STD_VERSION
-        if (!initcheck) {
+        // The profile key is wrapped below under the shared secret of the two
+        // PINs, and an unlock unwraps it with that secret only when the mode
+        // is STDPROFILE2 (password.cpp). Record the mode whenever a second PIN
+        // is set, not only at first setup, so a second PIN added in config
+        // mode is unwrapped with the secret it was wrapped with.
+        if (p2mode != STDPROFILE2) {
             // Default to standard profile
             p2mode = STDPROFILE2;
             okeeprom_eeset_2ndprofilemode(&p2mode);
-- 
2.55.0.windows.2

